# Iron-V local configuration
#
# Copy this file to .config (git-ignored) and change what you need. `make` reads the build
# profile (profiles/<PROFILE>.config, default light) and then .config, and turns both into
# build/<profile>/gen/config_gen.h, which overrides the defaults in src/config.h. Keys you
# leave out keep their defaults; .config applies to every profile you build.
# Format: KEY=VALUE, one per line, no quotes (everything after '=' is the value).

# Device name on the LAN: http://<HOSTNAME>.local (mDNS) and the DNS name on the SoftAP.
# Lowercase letters, digits and inner hyphens, up to 32 characters. Default: iron-v
#HOSTNAME=iron-v

# Setup access point (open network). Started at boot only while no Wi-Fi is saved; on a board
# with saved Wi-Fi, hold the BOOT button for 3 s to open it (it closes after 10 min unused,
# 30 min at most, or on the next long press, and the board rejoins its network).
# Default: IronV-AP on channel 1, started automatically.
#AP_SSID=IronV-AP
#AP_CHANNEL=1
#AP_AUTO_START=1

# Home network to join on the very first boot, so the setup portal can be skipped.
# Only seeds the board's storage (NVS) when it holds no Wi-Fi credentials; after that the
# portal and `sta connect`/`prov set` win. WPA2-PSK only; passphrase 8-63 characters.
# WARNING: the passphrase is compiled into build/<profile>/firmware.bin and readable from the flash
# (no flash encryption). Never share an image built with these set.
#STA_SSID=
#STA_PASSPHRASE=

# Extra modules (src/modules/<name>/) for every image you build, added to the profile's MODULES,
# e.g. the optional MQTT client (src/modules/mqtt/README.md). The profile keys themselves
# (MODULES, MAIN_STACK_MIN, POOL_*) are set in profiles/*.config only: .config also applies to
# the dev test build. A different module set or size is a profile of its own.
#MODULES_ADD=mqtt
